flowchart TD
  TITLE["YOUR MEMORY CARD — How Air Pressure Graph Points Are Prepared<br/><br/>Target for screen: max about 3000 points per run<br/>Two methods exist: WIDTH BUCKET and LTTB"]

  RULE["THE REAL SWITCH RULE in code<br/><br/>visual_max = 3000 usually<br/>threshold = min 400, visual_max = 400<br/><br/>IF raw_points > 400<br/>  use WIDTH BUCKET first, then LTTB<br/>ELSE<br/>  use real points, then LTTB only if needed<br/><br/>Important correction:<br/>Switch is NOT at 3000 or 5000.<br/>Switch is at about 400 points."]

  M1["METHOD 1 — WIDTH BUCKET<br/><br/>Used when: raw_points > 400<br/><br/>What it does:<br/>Split the whole run time into about 3000 time boxes<br/>In each box take AVG pressure<br/><br/>Result:<br/>Heavy data becomes about 3000 smooth points<br/><br/>Why we use it:<br/>LTTB alone on very dense data keeps too many spikes<br/>Bucket average gives smoother line"]

  M2["METHOD 2 — LTTB downsample<br/><br/>Full name: Largest Triangle Three Buckets<br/><br/>Used when:<br/>- small path: only if points > 3000<br/>- big path: always as safety after width_bucket<br/><br/>What it does:<br/>Keep start + end + important peaks/valleys<br/>Drop less important middle points<br/><br/>If points already <= 3000:<br/>LTTB does NOTHING and returns same points"]

  FLOW["COMMON FLOW FOR ONE LOG FILE<br/><br/>1. COUNT rows in pressure_sensor_data for that log_file_id<br/>2. Decide path using > 400 rule<br/>3. Prepare points<br/>4. Send chart_data to UI"]

  TITLE --> RULE --> M1 --> M2 --> FLOW
